# RULE 22 — SESSION BOOT ANNOUNCE + TIERED MODEL (owner 2026-07-22)

## New session (HARD)

On the **first assistant reply of every new conversation** (fresh chat / new agent session / no prior turns in this thread), the assistant MUST open with a visible line so Jorge knows rules just autoloaded:

```
NEW SESSION · rules autoloaded · tiered model in force (Rule 12) · continuous mode (Rule 32)
```

Immediately after that line, paste **CURRENT-LAW + MY HOPS** from `docs/lockdown/SESSION-ANNOUNCE-CURRENT-LAW-HOPS-2026-08-22.md` (brief bullets). **Omit CERTIFIED modules.** Then execute `docs/bus/INBOX-<SEAT>.md` TOP. Do **not** skip this on the first turn.

**Continuous mode (Rule 32):** never pause/idle after merges, PRs, Neon apply, or green CI — keep writing the next ranked FAIL in the same turn.

Continuing turns in the **same** conversation do **not** repeat the NEW SESSION banner — use the BLOCK progress header defined in **`.cursor/rules/24-module-completion-n-of-m.mdc` → "Session header"** instead. (This previously pointed at "Rule 20", which does not exist as a file; the header spec has always lived in 24.)

## Tiered model (ALWAYS — quality first, cost second)

Standing with `.cursor/rules/12-model-tiering.mdc`:

| Tier | Use for |
|------|---------|
| **Highest-capability** | Architecture/planning, ALL financial/accounting, migrations, RLS/schema, code-review + financial-agent, adversarial verify, ambiguous/high-stakes |
| **Mid-tier** | Routine feature code, UI wiring, non-financial backend, tests |
| **A — Frontier** | Money / schema / migrations / review / GUARD money |
| **B — Workhorse** | Feature UI, scoreboard, non-financial wiring |
| **C — Fast/cheap** | Mechanical class waves (Composer/Auto), docs, bulk |

Escalate the instant work touches money, schema, RLS, migrations, or linkage law. **When in doubt, escalate.**

Subagents: pick model by task tier (same table). Do not run financial/migration design on fast/cheap.

